s, contribuyendo a la hipertrigliceridemia.", "DEFICIT DE APO-V:El déficit de apo-V es un trastorno que afecta la unión de lipoproteínas a la lipoproteína lipasa, lo que puede llevar a quilomicronemia.", "DÉFICIT FAMILIAR DE LIPOPROTEÍNA LIPASA:El déficit familiar de lipoproteína lipasa es un trastorno autosómico recesivo que causa acumulación de quilomicrones en el plasma, resultando en hipertrigliceridemia y manifestaciones como xantomas y hepatomegalia.", "DÉFICIT DE APO C-II:El déficit de apo C-II es un trastorno autosómico recesivo que causa un déficit funcional de la lipoproteína lipasa, lo que lleva a la acumulación de quilomicrones y a niveles elevados de triglicéridos.", "DÉFICIT DE LIPASA HEPÁTICA:El déficit de lipasa hepática es un trastorno autosómico recesivo raro que interfiere con el catabolismo de las VLDL e IDL, contribuyendo a la hipertrigliceridemia.", "DÉFICIT DE APO-V:El déficit de apo-V es un trastorno que afecta la unión de las VLDL y los quilomicrones con la lipoproteína lipasa, lo que puede resultar en quilomicronemia.", "SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE MEDICINA INTERNA:The Sociedad Española de Medicina Interna, also known as the Spanish Society of Internal Medicine, is a prominent medical society in Spain dedicated to the field of internal medicine. This organization plays a crucial role in coordinating medical protocols and guidelines within the country. Among its contributions, the society has published protocols specifically addressing hypertriglyceridemia, which are referenced in various medical texts. Through its efforts, the Sociedad Española de Medicina Interna aims to enhance the quality of care and standardize practices in internal medicine across Spain.", "FENOFIBRATO:Fenofibrate is a medication primarily used to lower triglyceride levels in patients suffering from hypertriglyceridemia. Additionally, it is effective in reducing cholesterol levels and triglycerides in the blood, making it a common prescription for individuals with metabolic disorders.", "LOMITAPIDA:Lomitapide is a medication that can be prescribed for severe cases of hypertriglyceridemia.", "PLASMAFÉRESIS:Plasmapheresis is a medical procedure that is effective in rapidly normalizing triglyceride levels in patients experiencing severe hypertriglyceridemia and pancreatitis. It is particularly useful in acute situations where there is a need to quickly reduce triglyceride levels.", "HÁBITOS DE VIDA:Lifestyle habits refer to the daily behaviors and practices that can affect health, including diet and exercise.", "QUILOMICRONEMIAS:", "MARTÍN CUESTA HERNÁNDEZ:Martín Cuesta Hernández is a licensed physician and endocrinologist with a specialization in diabetes and new technologies. He has a robust background in both research and clinical practice, having worked in Madrid and Dublin. Currently, he serves as an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Clínico San Carlos in Madrid."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}